ernational attention for its high-stakes agenda, from trade and AI to Taiwan.', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/triumph-or-procrastination-experts-split-on-the-trump-xi-summit/'}, {'signal_id': 'fbaf8edfcbb8e5ad', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Rated Ready is Not Ready: What America’s Korea Exercises Actually Measure <p>&#8220;We want to stop the North Koreans as far from Pusan as we can. Block the main road as far north as possible. Contact General Church. If you can&#8217;t locate him, go to Taejon and beyond if you c', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/rated-ready-is-not-ready-what-americas-korea-exercises-actually-measure/'}, {'signal_id': 'eaa08a7ae327ebc5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Writing the Playbook: A Strategy and Doctrine for American Economic Security <p>In January, this article series opened with a blunt question: Economic statecraft is back, but is America ready?Driving the question, in part, was the fact that the United States had not yet articulat', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/writing-the-playbook-a-strategy-and-doctrine-for-american-economic-security/'}, {'signal_id': '2b78070b6d78fda8', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'What Will Hegseth’s “State of the Force” Reprise Reveal? <p>Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth is expected to convene a high-profile meeting of military personnel for a &#8220;State of the Force&#8221; address this week. Will it show the U.S. armed forces as healthy? The answer ma', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/what-will-hegseths-state-of-the-force-reprise-reveal/'}, {'signal_id': 'ef4bf871deff3866', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Unhedgeable Bet: What the Future Combat Systems Can Teach Us About Acquisition <p>The Pentagon describes Golden Dome for America as a&#160;&#8220;system of systems,&#8221; an integrated air and missile defense architecture that combines space-based sensors, orbital intercepto', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-unhedgeable-bet-what-the-future-combat-systems-can-teach-us-about-acquisition/'}, {'signal_id': '8b5baed2d8b2ce88', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Discipline of Refusal: Constitutional Concerns About Lawful Orders in the U.S. Military <p>Military doctrine gives officers a clear rule for manifestly unlawful orders: Refuse them. It offers no comparable rule when lawful action appears to threaten the constitutional structu', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-discipline-of-refusal-constitutional-concerns-about-lawful-orders-in-the-u-s-military/'}, {'signal_id': '835697eec5018469', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Manhattan Project Mindset: How Nuclear Analogies Are Steering AI Policy Off Course <p>Analogies for artificial intelligence abound. In recent years, analysts have likened the development of AI to the advent of electricity, the Industrial Revolution, contact with extraterrestr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-manhattan-project-mindset-how-nuclear-analogies-are-steering-ai-policy-off-course/'}, {'signal_id': '6e9f49ed30335284', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Why the Week’s Most Important Story Went Unwritten <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles fr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/why-the-weeks-most-important-story-went-unwritten/'}, {'signal_id': '5f06bd2df0b6d0ab', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Collective Defense in an Era of Tokens and Data Links <p>NATO&#8217;s Supreme Allied Commander Transformation, Adm. Pierre Vandier, returns to the studio to discuss how the alliance is continuously adapting to a new era of warfare driven by software, data, and uncrewed systems, a', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/collective-defense-in-an-era-of-tokens-and-data-links/'}, {'signal_id': 'd1016e746dc68955', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Speed to Fielding Is Not Speed to Combat Power <p>I spent more than 20 years in U.S. Army air defense, much of it in cramped control stations where the difference between a successful engagement and a catastrophic loss came down to the soldier at the console. The radar did its jo', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/speed-to-fielding-is-not-speed-to-combat-power/'}, {'signal_id': 'ec28565eed6fe31f', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Tracing the Future Soldier’s Tech Stack <p>Movies, shows, and books have long been at the forefront of imagining the future of war. If you were to picture the &#8220;future soldier,&#8221; you&#8217;d likely picture the genetically engineered super soldiers that have captivated &', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/tracing-the-future-soldiers-tech-stack/'}, {'signal_id': '21c9c6c673f0bf7e', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'North Korea’s Irregular Warfare After Ukraine <p>Pyongyang has a long history of conducting irregular warfare and asymmetric operations: Look no further than the 1968 Blue House raid or the 1996 submarine incursion as the most pressing examples. More often than not, North Korea f', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/north-koreas-irregular-warfare-after-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '259ceb6b0e5126a0', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Power, Prudence, and Restraint in Fénelon’s Telemachus <p>&#8220;If one is to judge by the fire and ardor with which this book is sought after, it is the most excellent of all books. Never were so many copies printed of any work; never were so many editions made of a single book;', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/power-prudence-and-restraint-in-fenelons-telemachus/'}, {'signal_id': 'b098b39f0b67ad91', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The New Signature Wounds: How Drone Warfare Is Reshaping the Injuries Veterans Bring Home <p>Traumatic brain injury became the signature wound of the post-9/11 wars because the battlefield changed. Improvised explosive devices changed the nature of American combat injuries. But t', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-new-signature-wounds-how-drone-warfare-is-reshaping-the-injuries-veterans-bring-home/'}, {'signal_id': '7e23b592960eb8bd', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'South Korea’s Deliberate Strategic Ambiguity on Taiwan <p>In 2021, Sungmin Cho wrote, &#8220;South Korea&#8217;s Taiwan Conundrum,&#8221; where he argued Seoul&#8217;s complex strategic position makes engagement on questions of involvement over a Taiwan contingency complicated. F', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/south-koreas-deliberate-strategic-ambiguity-on-taiwan/'}, {'signal_id': '1e3f2d5ffb0f815c', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Winning by the Rules: Optimizing Weapons Reviews in the Age of Technological Innovation <p>We spare the reader another detailed story from Ukraine to establish the now-familiar point that battlefield technology changes faster than militaries can acquire, review, and field it. The', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/winning-by-the-rules-optimizing-weapons-reviews-in-the-age-of-technological-innovation/'}, {'signal_id': '6b1638584d278fe5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Seoul Needs a Playbook for Hormuz, Ukraine, and What Comes Next <p>Earlier this month, President Donald Trump shared a Washington Post opinion piece on his social media, arguing that South Korea should send its Cheongung-II air-defense system to Ukraine. Additionally, the Trump a', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/seoul-needs-a-playbook-for-hormuz-ukraine-and-what-comes-next/'}, {'signal_id': '9bf925df61fedba8', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'What the End of Operation Inherent Resolve Means for Iraq and Syria <p>Operation Inherent Resolve is scheduled to end on Sept. 30, as remaining U.S. troops in northern Iraq complete their withdrawal. The United States formed Combined Joint Task Force &#8211; Operation Inherent Re', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/what-the-end-of-operation-inherent-resolve-means-for-iraq-and-syria/'}, {'signal_id': 'aadf64d78d30213a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Missed the Marque: Cyber Privateers Wanted, Compensation to Be Determined <p>Coverage of the new White House memorandum on combating cybercrime quickly reached the privateer label. CNN called the participants &#8220;cyber privateers,&#8221; invoking the image of government-sancti', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/missed-the-marque-cyber-privateers-wanted-compensation-to-be-determined/'}, {'signal_id': '42225fa90d1fc0ae', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Zelensky’s Perception Problem: Are New Partnerships a Solution? <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection o', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/zelenskys-perception-problem-are-new-partnerships-a-solution/'}, {'signal_id': 'd44ca2407cb37de2', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Washington’s Foreign Equity Bets Need Better Governance <p>What do a rare earth mine in Brazil and a graphite mine in Mozambique have in common? Both have received significant United States government funding. The rub? Neither was subject, when the financing was committed, to the', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/washingtons-foreign-equity-bets-need-better-governance/'}, {'signal_id': '6cd84c792977536e', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Only America Could Have Designed the Field Jacket <p>When the M-1943 field jacket was introduced at the height of World War II, it was a revolutionary garment. The jacket was the result of rigorous testing, input from an astonishingly diverse group of experts, and was produced by', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/only-america-could-have-designed-the-field-jacket/'}, {'signal_id': '6fa782126a98f2f9', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Pressure Points <p>Welcome to The Adversarial.&#160;Every other week, we&#8217;ll provide you with expert analysis on America&#8217;s greatest challengers: China, Russia, Iran, North Korea, and jihadists. Read more below.***IranSenior officials from Iran, Oman, and neighboring Gu', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/pressure-points/'}, {'signal_id': 'b35af368cba43d4e', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Why Eurasia, Not the Indo-Pacific, Matters Most in Next Phase of Taiwan Deterrence <p>Washington is preparing for the right war, but in the wrong theater. For years, U.S. strategic thinking has centered on the Indo&#8209;Pacific: the militarized atolls of the South China Sea, Chi', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/why-eurasia-not-the-indo-pacific-matters-most-in-next-phase-of-taiwan-deterrence/'}, {'signal_id': '0dfdfc89ad8a5bd8', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Latin America’s Balancing Act: Washington, Beijing, and the Post-Maduro Environment <p>The year 2026 has brought sweeping change to Latin America&#8217;s relationship with the United States. Following a major military buildup in the Caribbean and strikes against vessels suspected', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/latin-americas-balancing-act-washington-beijing-and-the-post-maduro-environment/'}, {'signal_id': '80e161497350eda0', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Reinventing Intelligence To Operate At Machine Speed <p>For almost a decade, the U.S. Intelligence Community (IC) has lived with a quiet anxiety: that the proliferation of open-source information, machine learning, and artificial intelligence would one day reshape its analytic en', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/reinventing-intelligence-to-operate-at-machine-speed'}, {'signal_id': '81044c7171d2b5e2', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "What Congress Can Learn From Vietnam About the War in Iran <p>“The American people don't know what the heck we're fighting for in Iran. He's [President Trump] never made it clear. He changes his mind day-to-day and minute-to-minute. This war must end. It must end. And make no mis", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-congress-can-learn-from-vietnam-about-the-war-in-iran'}, {'signal_id': 'c2a0899112d2e5b7', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Startups Are Now on the Front Lines <p>A recent Air Force contract to help screen small businesses applying for federal research funding reflects a growing national security concern: foreign access to American innovation.</p><p>Screening applicants is one part of that challenge. ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/startups-are-now-on-the-front-lines'}, {'signal_id': 'aa40e1848e011417', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Command We Must Fund <p>The Army's Armored Force was born in July 1940, a few weeks after France fell. No act of Congress created it, and no budget line funded it. The Chief of Staff ordered it into being, took the tanks from the infantry and the cavalry, and placed them unde", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-command-we-must-fund'}, {'signal_id': '1758759ee05ab6ab', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "China's Return to One-Man Rule <p>The U.S. will be holding mid-term elections on November 3, to elect the people’s representatives to enact laws, provide oversight and represent the people. In sharp contrast, China’s ruling Communist Party (CCP) announced that it formally expelle", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/china-return-one-man-rule'}, {'signal_id': 'cc09cf691ef60abd', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'In Its Race to Field AI, The Pentagon’s Testing Can’t Keep Up <p><a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/09/18/politics/us-military-ai-false-intelligence-china-ship" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CNN reported</a>, citing four sources familiar with the episode, that the U.S.', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/in-its-race-to-field-ai-the-pentagons-testing-cant-keep-up'}, {'signal_id': 'cfcda2cedd54f15b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Missing Dimension of Cyber Preparedness <p>The technical aspect of incident response can be immense. In extreme scenarios, such as the NotPetya incident in 2017, global organisations such as the shipping company Maersk found the speed and scale of the malware’s impact to be u', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-missing-dimension-of-cyber-preparedness'}, {'signal_id': 'd0688fd3517345b9', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "BLUF: The Next AI Problem for Intelligence Is Not the Model, It's the Manager <p>The Intelligence Community has decided AI agents are coming. It has not decided how they will be supervised, checked and held to analytic standards. In April, CIA Deputy Director Michael Ellis said a", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/bluf-the-next-ai-problem-for-intelligence-is-not-the-model-it-s-the-manager'}, {'signal_id': 'b0f661e1d265e2e1', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Fire Base Australia: Can America’s Southern Base Sustain a Pacific War? <p>American access to Australian bases is only as valuable as Australia’s ability to keep them operating under attack. For Washington, <a href="https://www.defence.gov.au/defence-activities/programs-initiativ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/fire-base-australia-can-americas-southern-base-sustain-a-pacific-war'}, {'signal_id': '2636724d659b320b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Coming Age of Robotic Warfare <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/france-defence-army-weaponry.jpg?id=68580393&amp;width=1200&amp;height=400&amp;coordinates=0%2C171%2C0%2C171" /><br /><br /><p>A battalion of armed robots moves against a unit of soldiers, ai', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-coming-age-of-robotic-warfare'}, {'signal_id': 'e23071c10fb2f7e7', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Hidden Cost of America’s War With Iran <p>“The [U.S. Naval Support Activity Bahrain] base and Fifth Fleet headquarters have been rendered largely inoperable for their original functions, with repairs estimated at $400 million… Chief of Naval Operations Admiral Daryl Caudle an', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/hidden-cost-war-with-iran'}, {'signal_id': 'dd10d7b644f8a031', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Command We Must Start <p><strong></strong>In 1928, Secretary of War Dwight Davis ordered the Army to assemble an experimental mechanized force of tanks, armored cars, and motorized infantry at Camp Meade, Maryland. It was disbanded within months. A second attempt was dissolve', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-command-we-must-start'}, {'signal_id': '43f6f5be3435ac91', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Cipher Brief’s 10th Threat Conference: Optimism, Urgency, and the Imperative to Act <p>Which came first: The Cloister at Sea Island, the Office of Strategic Services, or the CIA? The resort wins. The Cloister first opened in 1928, fourteen years before the OSS and nineteen be', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-cipher-briefs-10th-threat-conference-optimism-urgency-and-the-imperative-to-act'}, {'signal_id': '6114ee09bd6fceae', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Kids are Alright: U.S. Soft Power, Aid, and Youth in Africa <p><em>OPINION — A recent survey of African youth challenges conventional wisdom on foreign aid. Policymakers should take heed of their views as they design the future of U.S. foreign assistance to increase effective', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-kids-are-alright'}, {'signal_id': 'c6ca6333ccf272ad', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "F-35 Fallacy: Jets Alone Will Not Save Us <p>NATO Allies have bet the future of European skies on the world’s most sophisticated combat aircraft. NATO Allies are buying the world's most advanced fighter but many are neglecting vital investments in hard security, ground crews, and", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/f-35-fallacy-jets-alone-will-not-save-us'}, {'signal_id': 'fee7d3e35b4d3134', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The U.S. Military Has Much to Learn From Ukraine <p>“What does Ukraine really need? How do we make sure they're delivering what they actually need? And you know, right now those are air defense munitions, it's funding for drones, it's extended range artillery, electronic warfare,", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/why-americas-military-still-needs-its-allies'}, {'signal_id': '1a2041754d6a8495', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Terms We Must Set <p>On October 23, Russia's deputy prime minister said three tankers were at sea, that supply contracts were being finalized, and that volumes would rise to 1 million tons in December and could reach 3 million a month. A week earlier, the United States had wa", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-terms-we-must-set'}, {'signal_id': '15cbfb74f4b66b65', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Thirteenth Mile: This Is What Gray Zone War Looks Like <p>On the morning of October 23, the cargo ship Khoryv sent a distress call <a href="https://www.kyivpost.com/post/88003" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">13 nautical miles off Constanța</a>, Romania. Territorial', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-thirteenth-mile-this-is-what-gray-zone-war-looks-like'}, {'signal_id': '2bbcaebde45ce997', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Intelligence Community’s Missing Discipline <p>Economic statecraft has become a primary instrument of US national security, deployed with a frequency and ambition that outpaces the intelligence architecture built to support it. For sanctions, tariffs, investment screening, ex', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-intelligence-communitys-missing-discipline'}, {'signal_id': '535c3685a554e588', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'We’re Losing the Cognitive Space Race <p>Over the last century, modern medicine achieved a historic feat. We increased the human lifespan by 33%. But at the same time, we completely failed to defend our brain healthspan. Today, a silent gap of 15 to 30 years exists between the ti', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/were-losing-the-cognitive-space-race'}, {'signal_id': '4b15e2360fb8530e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Russia Never Left the International Financial System. It Built a Way Back In. <p>A7’s OpenAI prompt was six words long: "Translate [name] to [language]. Answer only translated text."</p><p>Developer code leaked in 2025 from A7—the Kremlin-linked payment network designated by Trea', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/russia-never-left-the-international-financial-system-it-built-a-way-back-in'}, {'signal_id': 'fcc142ead8a66abb', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Turkey Has Outsourced Its Censorship to American Companies <p>Earlier this month, Sky News correspondent <a href="https://ground.news/article/sky-news-reporter-alex-crawfords-x-account" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Alex Crawford</a> got a notice from X: her account w', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/turkey-has-outsourced-its-censorship-to-american-companies'}, {'signal_id': 'e1b2c0d145ded66c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Technology Is Outrunning the Way We Fight <p>The United States is racing to field AI and autonomous systems. It is not racing to figure out how to fight with them. This imbalance between technology and concepts is widening a gap the U.S. is ill prepared to close. Ukraine has show', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/technology-is-outrunning-the-way-we-fight'}, {'signal_id': '15b847110bac0873', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Hybrid Threats: Why Awareness Must Transcend Individual Cyberattacks <p>Every October, Cybersecurity Awareness Month puts practical security measures in the spotlight. Can an employee recognize a phishing email? Will someone pause before clicking a suspicious link? Are passwords ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/hybrid-threats-why-awareness-must-transcend-individual-cyberattacks'}, {'signal_id': '46024bc6e9fc668a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'America\'s Counter-Drone Authority Is Real, The Capacity Isn\'t Yet <p>Here is a number worth sitting with: federal teams seized roughly <a href="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fbi-counter-drone-school-double-capacity-woodward" target="_blank" title="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fb', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/america-s-counter-drone-authority-is-real-the-capacity-isn-t-yet'}, {'signal_id': '217c50e76268bc84', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The U.S. Army’s Pacific Strategy Depends on Allies <p>“We never fight alone. We've never done that. You can go all the way back to the days of Revolutionary War. The United States has never gone into conflict on its own. We've always built coalitions. We've always involved partne", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-u-s-armys-pacific-strategy-depends-on-allies'}, {'signal_id': '612051baeeba5542', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Hidden Risks of AI-Powered Intelligence <p><span>Picture an </span>intelligent analyst's screen. Data about troop movements, a port closure, a terrorist attack, or a weapons transfer sits at the center of a clean interface, with a confidence indicator glowing green. Two hundr", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-hidden-risks-of-ai-powered-intelligence'}, {'signal_id': '67fbdeb10f8d3e21', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What a Russian Hybrid Attack Might Look Like <p>Russia has demonstrated a growing willingness to use hybrid tactics – including sabotage, cyberattacks, information operations, and the use of deniable or “throwaway” agents – to create disruption and uncertainty across Europe. This', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-a-russian-hybrid-attack-might-look-like'}, {'signal_id': 'aabdf5a0d915c66e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Muhammad bin Salman’s Humbling and the Return of the Ottomans <p>The Houthis bloodied Saudi Crown Prince Muhammad bin Salman’s nose—again—with their deadly, cruel, but effective attacks on Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport last week. The strikes are the latest in a serie', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/muhammad-bin-salmans-humbling-and-the-return-of-the-ottomans'}, {'signal_id': '1768a2a205f8c24a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Day We Cannot Choose <p>Washington made three decisions this week, and none of them has an end date. On the night of October 14, Ukrainian units in the field found that their Starshield terminals had been capped at a speed, 160 kilometers an hour by the published figure, 70 b', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-day-we-cannot-choose'}, {'signal_id': 'f00df7d66b8e78ad', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'This Veterans Day, Honor Service Members’ Character by Restoring Trust in the Institutions They Serve <p>Veterans Day should mark an opportunity for leaders to begin the difficult work of rebuilding trust in U.S. institutions at home and abroad.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://w', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163904/veterans-day-restore-trust-institutions/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=veterans-day-restore-trust-institutions'}, {'signal_id': '75ef6dda6bea43df', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'What a Democratic Congress is Likely to Do on Foreign Policy <p>What actions the incoming House and Senate majorities may take on the Iran war, tariffs, foreign assistance, and more.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/163835/democratic-congress-likely-do-foreig', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163835/democratic-congress-likely-do-foreign-policy/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=democratic-congress-likely-do-foreign-policy'}, {'signal_id': 'db29e963e1ea0741', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'An Urgent and Existential Threat: The Climate Crisis Is Also a Rule of Law Emergency <p>Legal frameworks that were not developed to respond to the climate crisis must quickly adapt to solve the justice problems they create.\xa0</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/1', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163602/climate-crisis-rule-of-law-emergency/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=climate-crisis-rule-of-law-emergency'}, {'signal_id': '762d2c231f7b923e', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'America’s Civic Renewal Is Here, And Veterans Are Leading It <p>This Veterans Day should remind us that Americans do not have to agree on everything to build something together.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/163906/americas-civic-renewal-veterans-leading/"', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163906/americas-civic-renewal-veterans-leading/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=americas-civic-renewal-veterans-leading'}, {'signal_id': 'ad0774a3d7395cc0', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: November 11, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio yesterday said that the Trump administrati', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/164111/early-edition-november-11-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-november-11-2026'}, {'signal_id': 'b4d07c16a2b03fa1', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Exclusive: Judge Bars DOJ Attorney from Appearing in Case: “Deliberate Attempt to Mislead the Court” <p>Federal judge accused DOJ attorneys of “prima facie Rule 11 violations,” barred an attorney from future appearances in case, launching review of other DOJ attorneys. </p>\n<p>Th', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163989/judge-bars-doj-attorney-thomas-price/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=judge-bars-doj-attorney-thomas-price'}, {'signal_id': '9682222f8b11e4cb', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Getting Serious About Accountability in the United States <p>The fundamental principle that no person is above the law is an American value and a prerequisite to a functioning democracy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/164034/getting-serious-accountability-u', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/164034/getting-serious-accountability-united-states/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=getting-serious-accountability-united-states'}, {'signal_id': '3cfa640c6a3d99dc', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Syria on the Road to Trials of Chemical Weapons Use: Attributing an Attack Does Not Prove Individual Criminal  Responsibility <p>Syrian prosecutors should not bring chemical weapons charges against any detainee unless they can identify a specific incident and evidence linking the', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/160365/syria-trials-chemical-weapons-use/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=syria-trials-chemical-weapons-use'}, {'signal_id': 'ab27bd0e2794fb03', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'COP31 and the U.S. Retreat from Global Climate Leadership <p>Expect COP31 to be judged less by its concrete outcomes than by who steps into the space the United States has left behind.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/163811/cop31-us-retreat-global-climate-le', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163811/cop31-us-retreat-global-climate-leadership/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=cop31-us-retreat-global-climate-leadership'}, {'signal_id': '9944dde017bf4e77', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'The Nord Stream Prosecution: Immunity, Military Objectives, and Superior Orders <p>Top experts examine international legal issues in German efforts to prosecute Ukraine military members for the 2022 Nord Stream sabotage.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/16388', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163881/germany-ukraine-nord-stream-prosecution/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=germany-ukraine-nord-stream-prosecution'}, {'signal_id': '7511ada3869cbc10', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Veterans, Families, and Life After Military Service: Q&amp;A with RAND Experts For veterans, leaving the U.S. military can open new doors and raise new questions. In this Q&amp;A, Carrie Farmer and Rajeev Ramchand share what RAND's research reveals about life after military servi", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/veterans-families-and-life-after-military-service-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': '699151b3a720c899', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Preparedness for the AI Era Requires a Reserve of Critical Workers If governments or employers assume that permanent AI automation is right around the corner, vital training and career pipelines could collapse. We could find ourselves without enough people to perform work essenti', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/preparedness-for-the-ai-era-requires-a-reserve-of-critical.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a2e2626dbe7e57d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Lessons from L.A. on Transfer Taxes San Francisco voters have a new proposition on real estate transfer taxes to consider. Aspects of and arguments for the new Prop 1 closely mirror the debate over Los Angeles' Measure ULA, a 2022 ballot initiative that established a similar tran", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/lessons-from-la-on-transfer-taxes.html'}, {'signal_id': 'fa820f34bcc199f0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Why Employers Can't Tame Health Costs Price transparency alone isn’t helping employers rein in health care costs. What will it take to give them real leverage—and overcome the barriers of today’s system?", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/why-employers-cant-tame-health-costs.html'}, {'signal_id': '27c968e09255c3ca', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "America's Least Bad Option in Iran In Iran, the United States could return to a full-scale bombing campaign, walk away from the conflict, or stick with the current approach. Staying the course almost certainly will not bring quick results but it is strategically prudent.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/americas-least-bad-option-in-iran.html'}, {'signal_id': '1360f15fbaf3d074', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Why Quick Compensation Hasn't Replaced Eaton Fire Lawsuits—So Far A review of Southern California Edison's direct-payment program finds that it has paid claimants much faster, but it hasn't become a broad substitute for lawsuits.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/why-quick-compensation-hasnt-replaced-eaton-fire-lawsuits.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b8e2180ad066e052', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Missing Link in Drug Policy: Why Whole-System Reform Is Stalling The UK has made progress toward a whole-system approach to drug policy, but unclear accountability and persistent stigma are stalling reform.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/the-missing-link-in-drug-policy-why-whole-system-reform.html'}, {'signal_id': '1c27b342495b14b7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "A Better Way to Use Criminal Records in Hiring Employers want to know whether an applicant is likely to commit another crime, possibly on the job. But the screening rules many of them use are often about as accurate as a coin toss, in part because they're based on data that don't", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/a-better-way-to-use-criminal-records-in-hiring.html'}, {'signal_id': '7eb450727724ee69', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "This Is How to End Israel's Isolation The hope of many Israelis and Israel's supporters around the world is that elections on Oct. 27 will usher in a new government and slow the slide into greater isolation. New leadership could ease Israel's isolation temporarily. But will a dee", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/this-is-how-to-end-israels-isolation.html'}, {'signal_id': '1f82f8da9de912b0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Biosecurity in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Steph Guerra The question that drives Steph Guerra's work at RAND may be one of the most consequential for this moment in the AI era: How can we harness the full potential of AI for science and medicine—but also ensure it never helps any", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/biosecurity-in-the-age-of-ai-qa-with-steph-guerra.html'}, {'signal_id': '510596eafa31042f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'From Strategic Logic to Practical Implementation: A Phased Agenda for U.S.-ROK Shipbuilding Cooperation U.S.-ROK cooperation on shipbuilding should be structured so that it strengthens U.S. maritime industrial capacity, makes commercial sense for Korean shipbuilders, and survives', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/from-strategic-logic-to-practical-implementation-a.html'}, {'signal_id': 'c5904b48ce512115', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "9/11's Forgotten Lesson Twenty-five years later, 9/11's lessons are still contested, except the simplest: the United States mistook quiet for peace. And it is doing so again.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/911s-forgotten-lesson.html'}, {'signal_id': '645e5c8159c45b3c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Schools, Cell Phones, and AI: Q&amp;A with Melissa Kay Diliberti Melissa Kay Diliberti, an associate policy researcher at RAND, discusses recent findings from RAND that can help parents and policymakers better understand what challenges schools are up against.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/schools-cell-phones-and-ai-qa-with-melissa-kay-diliberti.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f0a6bf01926bc40a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Netanyahu May Have Ignored a Dire Warning. Israel Ignores the Deeper Threat. Israel's strategy in Gaza is only keeping Hamas in power: deterred, but not replaced, with no real alternative given a chance. A different outcome calls for a different approach.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/nentanyahu-may-have-ignored-a-dire-warning-israel-ignores-the.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b489a15858be84c1', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Never Underestimate the Houthis Yemen's Houthi rebels are in a position to shape the next phase of the conflict between the United States and Iran if they attempt to renew their blockade of the Bab al-Mandab Strait. And no one should assume that a deal with Iran will bind what th", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/never-underestimate-the-houthis.html'}, {'signal_id': '19d8064c433770cf', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Preserving Jobs and Tax Revenue in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Carter Price Carter Price, a mathematician at RAND and co-director of the RAND Von Furstenberg Family Budget Model Initiative, discusses ways to rebalance the tax code so that it doesn't incentivize employers to repla", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/preserving-jobs-and-tax-revenue-in-the-age-of-ai-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2d02311d1d9e0e7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Recent Rise of Women Gun Owners In recent years, women made up almost half of all new gun owners, a striking shift from the historical norm, when women accounted for about a quarter of them. And the uptick is widespread across geographic and demographic subgroups.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/the-recent-rise-of-women-gun-owners.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a9dc8988cf7146c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Who Benefits from Education Savings Accounts? Q&amp;A with Susha Roy Tens of thousands of American families use state-funded education savings accounts for their children's education. How exactly do these accounts work? Who benefits from them? And how do they affect education fun", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/who-benefits-from-education-savings-accounts.html'}, {'signal_id': '480b7da85115059d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Getting a Security Clearance Doesn't Have to Be So Intimidating: Q&amp;A with Sina Beaghley The security clearance process can be difficult and time-consuming but the government has made big strides in improving it. Sina Beaghley, a senior international and defense researcher at ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/getting-a-security-clearance-doesnt-have-to-be-so-intimidating.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2b8719ed5ca0a96', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': '25 Years After 9/11: Lessons for Securing the Homeland Reflecting on 25 years since the September 11 terror attacks, RAND experts answer questions about protecting soft targets, the role of the TSA, mitigating risks from emerging technologies, and more.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/25-years-after-911-lessons-for-securing-the-homeland.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f4b89699209b2372', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Where the Russia-Ukraine peace talks stand after Abu Dhabi <p>Our experts unpack what this week\'s US-brokered talks between Russia and Ukraine mean for European security and the prospects for peace.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthink', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/where-the-russia-ukraine-peace-talks-stand-after-abu-dhabi/'}, {'signal_id': '7f07370306af947e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukraine’s new drone blitz cuts Russian oil refining capacity by 30 percent <p>Ukraine has renewed attacks on Putin's energy industry in recent days, conducting a series of powerful strikes that have reportedly cut Russian oil refining capacity by around 30 percent and sparked fue", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-new-drone-blitz-cuts-russian-oil-refining-capacity-by-30-percent/'}, {'signal_id': 'f597f91d3c9e701b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Europe sees surge in suspected Russian hybrid warfare incidents <p>Europe has witnessed a surge in suspected Russian hybrid warfare incidents in recent weeks. This is fueling concerns that Vladimir Putin is escalating his intimidation campaign against Ukraine’s partners, writes M', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/europe-sees-surge-in-suspected-russian-hybrid-warfare-incidents/'}, {'signal_id': '5d9fa876c790088c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nick Clegg on Trump, Silicon Valley, and Big Tech’s political shift <p>Nick Clegg, former British deputy prime minister and Meta’s former president of global affairs, joins Frederick Kempe for a candid conversation about his time in government.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://ww', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-with-frederick-kempe/nick-clegg-on-trumo-silicon-valley-and-big-techs-political-shift/'}, {'signal_id': '0b707e3489cb71c1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Materials matter: Managing critical commodities for the next-generation energy economy <p>As economies electrify, demand will grow for materials such as copper, steel, and durable plastics that underpin the energy system. Managing these materials' supply risks will be crucial to ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/materials-matter-managing-critical-commodities-for-the-next-generation-energy-economy/'}, {'signal_id': 'f0089138a9a025eb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Water infrastructure at the Mediterranean’s inflection point: Financing resilience for an industrializing, digitalizing region <p>Increasing demand, driven by industrialization and digital infrastructure, requires a region-wide rethinking of water planning and financing mechanism', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/water-infrastructure-at-the-mediterraneans-inflection-point/'}, {'signal_id': '3bc53481eefaa84c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What students got right about the $6 billion Binance hack, and how they would prevent the next one <p>A year before the largest cryptocurrency theft in history, students at an Atlantic Council cyber strategy competition encountered an eerily similar scenario.</p>\n<p>The post <a h', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-students-got-right-about-the-6-billion-binance-hack-and-how-they-would-prevent-the-next-one/'}, {'signal_id': '9548d168023b5709', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Berlin: What Germans most want to know about the post-midterms United States <p>Germany faces even more pressure to lead European security amid uncertainty over the Trump administration\'s post-midterm Russia policy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcounc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-germans-most-want-to-know-about-the-post-midterms-united-states/'}, {'signal_id': '703b23f5cba07571', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The National Interest: On Immigration, the US Is Not Europe—Unless It Chooses to Be <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-on-immigration-the-us-is-not-europe-unless-it-chooses-to-be/">Charai for', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-on-immigration-the-us-is-not-europe-unless-it-chooses-to-be/'}, {'signal_id': '26a4069e351d54f3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dollar Dominance Monitor cited in a Project Syndicate article on the yuan’s growing role in international trade <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countri', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-developing-cbdcs-2-3/'}, {'signal_id': 'df72a58dbbcc7043', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'CBDC Tracker cited in a CEPR paper on Europe’s plans for retail and wholesale payments <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-de', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-developing-cbdcs-2-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'c4b562f5ec37fa1b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky and Piasecki quoted in a China Daily article on the impact of the 2027 budget and debt ceiling negotiations on global financial markets <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-9/'}, {'signal_id': '0c2de8dd923e5461', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield interviewed by Radio Télévision Suisse (RTS) about the US midterm elections <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollar', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-8/'}, {'signal_id': '4491c55cffcf71a7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in a South China Morning Post article discussing how Congress could constrain Trump’s agenda following the 2026 US midterm elections <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-7/'}, {'signal_id': 'edf2ba8bd364e9a1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani’s article on the future of the digital euro cited in an OMFIF article <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarizatio', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-6/'}, {'signal_id': '7d3727850d11ec4a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield interviewed by France Culture (Radio France) on how Trump’s economic policies could affect Republican support in the 2026 midterm elections <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-5/'}, {'signal_id': '2363667b922201e6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Piasecki’s research on Venezuela’s debt restructuring cited in a Congressional Research Service report <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-infl', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-4/'}, {'signal_id': 'c781768a129490e2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani quoted in an AFP article on the G20 foreign ministers’ meeting in Atlanta <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollariz', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-3/'}, {'signal_id': '5a39d271cf3a453f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in a South China Morning Post article on how Democrats could push to rein in Trump’s tariffs and give Congress more control over trade policy <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'e6af0cdfa3071acb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Dubai: After the midterms, allies see both US resilience and unreliability <p>In the Middle East, Europe, and Asia, allies are impressed by US democratic resilience but worried about policy predictability.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/con', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dispatch-from-dubai-after-the-midterms-allies-see-both-us-resilience-and-unreliability/'}, {'signal_id': 'f051b77c4c916b09', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why Belgrade’s new government should not let the Vertical Gas Corridor slip <p>Serbia’s incoming government should stay the course on the Vertical Gas Corridor to advance economic growth, energy security, and market transparency in line with the Student List’s reform agenda.</p>\n', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/why-belgrades-new-government-should-not-let-the-vertical-gas-corridor-slip/'}, {'signal_id': '7ca16578abb7fe5b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin wants peace talks. He doesn’t want peace. <p>The Russian president is using negotiations, including the upcoming US-Ukraine-Russia talks in Abu Dhabi, to buy time and extract concessions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/putin-wants-peace-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/putin-wants-peace-talks-he-doesnt-want-peace/'}, {'signal_id': 'e4081afe3420a4a2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The six strategic mistakes that led to US defeat in Afghanistan <p>Twenty-five years on, the United States\' defeat in Afghanistan appears less inevitable than the result of decisions that undermined its ability to prevent the Taliban\'s resurgence.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-six-strategic-mistakes-that-led-to-us-defeat-in-afghanistan/'}, {'signal_id': 'aa05b74995a1ec7b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'To settle Russia’s Ukraine war, Europe needs to let Kyiv in. Trump can help (really). <p>Any deal to end the war in Ukraine must fix a date for Kyiv to join the EU, but countless hurdles stand in the way. Washington has the leverage to help Brussels clear them—if it can use that ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/to-settle-russias-ukraine-war-europe-needs-to-let-kyiv-in-trump-can-help-really/'}, {'signal_id': 'd58e68beb3bd8752', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Not quite mercenaries: How Russia lures thousands of foreigners to fight in its war on Ukraine <p>Many of Russia\'s foreign recruits were coerced into service due to vulnerable legal or financial statuses. What should become of them?</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticco', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/not-quite-mercenaries-how-russia-lures-thousands-of-foreigners-to-fight-in-its-war-on-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '55bf973475fe904f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin suffers Balkan setbacks as Russia struggles to retain influence <p>Russia’s recent setbacks in the Balkans are a reminder of the foreign policy challenges facing the Kremlin as the full-scale invasion of Ukraine approaches a sixth year with no end in sight, writes Michael G', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putin-suffers-balkan-setbacks-as-russia-struggles-to-retain-influence/'}, {'signal_id': 'f6458a64ac188ee9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Last week’s brief Ukraine ceasefire did not stop Russian attacks on civilians <p>A recent humanitarian ceasefire around the southern Ukrainian city of Oleshky made it possible to evacuate hundreds of residents, but Russian attacks on civilians elsewhere in Ukraine continue, write', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/last-weeks-brief-ukraine-ceasefire-did-not-stop-russian-attacks-on-civilians/'}, {'signal_id': 'e8ab9ff105e60eb4', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Washington should broaden its Shia outreach in Iraq. Muqtada al-Sadr is a case study. <p>Conversations with several Sadrists reveal a movement preparing to fill a leadership vacuum in Iraq—and engage with the US.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/mena', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/washington-should-broaden-its-shia-outreach-in-iraq-muqtada-al-sadr-is-a-case-study/'}, {'signal_id': '30a855686c4c1940', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Post: Can Israeli leaders afford not to change after the American midterm results? <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-post-can-israeli-leaders-afford-not-to-change-after-the-american-mi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-post-can-israeli-leaders-afford-not-to-change-after-the-american-midterm-results/'}, {'signal_id': '64df3e43ad8ae877', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'As Gen Z asserts itself in Serbia and Albania, the upside for the West is far greater than the headaches <p>The West has an opening to advance democratic values and foreign policy alignment in the Balkans.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/as-gen', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/as-gen-z-asserts-itself-in-serbia-and-albania-the-upside-for-the-west-is-far-greater-than-the-headaches/'}, {'signal_id': '0042092f79ca5a88', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why this US midterm was unusually important for the Middle East <p>Midterm losses may reduce the immediate risk of renewed US strikes on Iran, but could drive Trump toward escalation in the months ahead.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/why-this', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/why-this-us-midterm-was-unusually-important-for-the-middle-east/'}, {'signal_id': 'fd30df6bfedd98f7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What the midterms will (and won’t) change for US foreign policy <p> Our experts explain where the power shift could change foreign policy—and where it won’t.\xa0</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-the-midterms-will-and-wont-chan', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-the-midterms-will-and-wont-change-for-us-foreign-policy/'}, {'signal_id': 'def8585680f48b41', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: The Midterm Verdict and the Test of American Leadership <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-midterm-verdict-and-the-test-of-american-leadership/"', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-midterm-verdict-and-the-test-of-american-leadership/'}, {'signal_id': 'c9820844989a7507', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Experts react: Democrats just swept the US midterms. Here’s what it means for the world. <p>Our experts assess the global implications of the midterm elections on issues ranging from energy and the economy to US foreign policy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/experts-react-democrats-just-swept-the-us-midterms-heres-what-it-means-for-the-world/'}, {'signal_id': 'c3dc3f0c4c083ce7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The midterms are done. Time for the fiscal clashes to begin. <p>The Democrats’ victory in the 2026 US midterm elections sets the stage for major showdowns on the federal budget and the debt ceiling.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-midterms-are-done-time-for-the-fiscal-clashes-to-begin/'}, {'signal_id': '51d418ea744e28a7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'A $6 billion hack in a season of AI anxiety <p>A $6.3 billion Binance hack and AI-assisted discoveries of software vulnerabilities made unsettling headlines. But not everything is as new or terrifying as it seems.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/eco', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/a-6-billion-hack-in-a-season-of-ai-anxiety/'}, {'signal_id': 'ac2e247d95eba903', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Europe must weigh rising Ukraine costs against higher price of Russian victory <p>If Russia succeeds in overrunning an underfunded and exhausted Ukraine, the consequences for Europe will be catastrophic and the price tag of stopping an emboldened Putin will dwarf the current cost', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/europe-must-weigh-rising-cost-of-supporting-ukraine-against-far-higher-price-of-russian-victory/'}, {'signal_id': '9ed1a9e43b8f21a1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'A strong defense industry may be Ukraine’s best security guarantee <p>Ukrainians have little faith in written guarantees and are well aware that nobody is going to fight Russia on their behalf. Instead, their most realistic security guarantee is a strong Ukrainian military backed', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/a-strong-defense-industry-may-be-ukraines-best-security-guarantee/'}, {'signal_id': '06f47ff5b9196be7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'New Palestinian leaders will need more than an electoral mandate to govern <p>The 2027 Palestinian elections will only give new leaders the authority to govern if they can control finances and security and rival factions agree to accept the results.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/new-palestinian-leaders-will-need-more-than-an-electoral-mandate-to-govern/'}, {'signal_id': '48c0a4431fdad63a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Religion as statecraft: What a decade of research reveals about the geopolitics of religious soft power <p>The post-Cold War assumption that international politics was converging toward a secular liberal framework in which religion would play at most a marginal role has not survi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/religion-as-statecraft-what-a-decade-of-research-reveals-about-the-geopolitics-of-religious-soft-power/'}, {'signal_id': '2f21c01cb61a67c8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Abu Dhabi: America votes—and the world holds its breath <p>The world is showing more interest than ever in the US midterm elections, and with good reason given how the results could affect Trump\'s foreign policy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dispatch-from-abu-dhabi-america-votes-and-the-world-holds-its-breath/'}, {'signal_id': '5ad7af3ef0557cfc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Scowcroft Strategy Scorecard: Grading Canada’s second-ever national security strategy <p>For only the second time in its history, Canada has a new national security strategy. Does it match the clarity with which Prime Minister Mark Carney has described the challenges the country ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/scorecard/scowcroft-strategy-scorecard-grading-canadas-second-ever-national-security-strategy/'}, {'signal_id': '305d78c1be93e255', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: The Iran War: What Victory Must Achieve. <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-iran-war-what-victory-must-achieve/">Charai for The Jerusalem Strate', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-iran-war-what-victory-must-achieve/'}, {'signal_id': '3f21234d817e4e7a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How to prevent an energy quarantine of Taiwan <p>An all-of-the-above energy strategy in Taiwan can help the United States and allies deter a Chinese energy quarantine of the island.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how-to-prevent-an-energy-quarantine-of-taiwan/'}, {'signal_id': '72a3e6dde5a2e9ab', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'As energy prices threaten inflation again, Lagarde’s European Central Bank legacy offers lessons <p>Christine Lagarde\'s European Central Bank legacy reflects strong crisis management and efforts to strengthen the euro, but a mixed record on inflation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="htt', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/as-energy-prices-threaten-inflation-again-lagardes-european-central-bank-legacy-offers-lessons/'}, {'signal_id': 'c5f106fd0eb26daa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Washington Tariff & Trade Letter on the US’s use of Smoot-Hawley law to impose tariffs on Canada <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-on-the-uss-use-of-smoot-hawley-law-to-impose-tariffs-on-canada/'}, {'signal_id': '8b2a0910ab390025', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in National Post on the implications of USMCA uncertainty on long-term North American supply chain security <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-im', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-implications-of-usmca-uncertainty-on-long-term-north-american-supply-chain-security/'}, {'signal_id': '5544debd93d9e27e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Reforma on how China benefits from USMCA uncertainty and fragmentation <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-fragmentation/'}, {'signal_id': 'd6db05d976be6e1f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Financial Review on the USMCA renegotiating process and the implications of uncertainty for the trade bloc <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-financial-review-on-t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-financial-review-on-the-usmca-renegotiating-process-and-the-implications-of-uncertainty-for-the-trade-bloc/'}, {'signal_id': 'fb7557ba434605b2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Barron’s on how Canada’s economy can sustain disruptions and mixed signals on trade from US <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-barrons-on-how-canadas-economy-can-s', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-barrons-on-how-canadas-economy-can-sustain-disruptions-and-mixed-signals-on-trade-from-us/'}, {'signal_id': '65c639722093fd44', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nikoladze quoted in The Christian Science Monitor on the effectiveness of tariffs authorized by the Russia Sanctions Act of 2026 <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-the-christian-sci', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-the-christian-science-monitor-on-the-effectiveness-of-tariffs-authorized-by-the-russia-sanctions-act-of-2026/'}, {'signal_id': '0aea3c2432b0f44c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nikoladze quoted in Washington Monthly on the Russia Sanctions Act of 2026’s implications for existing Russia-related sanctions <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-washington-monthly', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-washington-monthly-on-the-russia-sanctions-act-of-2026s-implications-for-existing-russia-related-sanctions/'}, {'signal_id': '7c343a0c3372803a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'CBDC Tracker cited in American Institute for Economic Research report on how countries are exploring the use of digital currencies <p>Explore the CBDC Tracker here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/cbdc-tracker-cited-in-american-i', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/cbdc-tracker-cited-in-american-institute-for-economic-research-report-on-how-countries-are-exploring-the-use-of-digital-currencies/'}, {'signal_id': '2321f3f198ede3ff', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani cited in American Institute for Economic Research report on the volume of e-CNY transactions by 2025 <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chhangani-cited-in-american-institute-for-economic-rese', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chhangani-cited-in-american-institute-for-economic-research-report-on-the-volume-of-e-cny-transactions-by-2025/'}, {'signal_id': 'f5ec9d1638ca5e77', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Donovan and Ezratty cited in RUSI journal on the Chinese and Russian material support for Iran’s war efforts <p>Read the full publication here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/donovan-and-ezratty-cited-in-rusi-journal-on-the-chin', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/donovan-and-ezratty-cited-in-rusi-journal-on-the-chinese-and-russian-material-support-for-irans-war-efforts/'}, {'signal_id': 'd4a66a2f2d4c4cbc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'De Kruijf cited in Centre for Economic Policy Research report on the euro’s constraints as dollar flight increases <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/de-kruijf-cited-in-centre-for-economic-policy-resea', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/de-kruijf-cited-in-centre-for-economic-policy-research-report-on-the-euros-constraints-as-dollar-flight-increases/'}, {'signal_id': 'e655d3fddd1d39ee', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Donovan and Ezratty cited in Foreign Policy on Russia’s and China’s material assistance for Iran’s war efforts <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/donovan-and-ezratty-cited-in-foreign-policy-on-russias-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/donovan-and-ezratty-cited-in-foreign-policy-on-russias-and-chinas-material-assistance-for-irans-war-efforts/'}, {'signal_id': '526113215fd7d719', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani quoted in Arabian Gulf Business Insight on the implications of Saudi Arabia’s exit from mBridge <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chhangani-quoted-in-arabian-gulf-business-insight-on-the-imp', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chhangani-quoted-in-arabian-gulf-business-insight-on-the-implications-of-saudi-arabias-exit-from-mbridge/'}, {'signal_id': 'a4f988a46237e286', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Goodwin-Groen quoted in Rzeczpospolita on the importance of modernized payment systems and digital currencies for development <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goodwin-groen-quoted-in-rzeczpospolita-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goodwin-groen-quoted-in-rzeczpospolita-on-the-importance-of-modernized-payment-systems-and-digital-currencies-for-development/'}, {'signal_id': '49dffb503a71f45f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Tannebaum interviewed on Bloomberg Surveillance on US-Ukraine relations and Russian peace talks <p>Listen to the full podcast episode here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-interviewed-on-bloomberg-surveillance-on-us-ukr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-interviewed-on-bloomberg-surveillance-on-us-ukraine-relations-and-russian-peace-talks/'}, {'signal_id': '341b1ea3a5724c2c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Libya’s maritime deal with Turkey may be the key to reunification <p>The deal, and the rise of Saddam Haftar, represent a new approach to Libya’s divided domestic politics and foreign relations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/libyas-mari', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/libyas-maritime-deal-with-turkey-may-be-the-key-to-reunification/'}, {'signal_id': '6214ccc141678b8c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The relationship between female leadership, political freedom, and the rule of law <p>How is female leadership in public service associated with two institutional outcomes: political freedom and rule of law? Understanding the broader implications of women’s representation in lead', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-relationship-between-female-leadership-political-freedom-and-the-rule-law/'}, {'signal_id': 'b8e9d8132e49afe6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine’s drone defenses debunk the myth of inevitable Russian victory <p>Ukraine’s emergence since 2022 as a drone superpower has made international headlines, but the role of drone-based air defenses on the battlefield has not yet received as much attention as it arguably deser', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-drone-defenses-debunk-the-myth-of-inevitable-russian-victory/'}, {'signal_id': 'c18fe6e50c050bd1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'France’s protests are playing into Le Pen’s hands <p>Protests have shifted France\'s national debate toward restoring order, a narrative that aligns closely with Marine Le Pen’s and the French right’s messaging.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/f', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/frances-protests-are-playing-into-le-pens-hands/'}, {'signal_id': '8f192a81cd682464', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin’s quest to reclaim ‘historical Russian lands’ is a recipe for endless war <p>Russian President Vladimir Putin\'s insistence that Ukraine is "historically Russian land" reveals the extent of his imperial ambitions and represents a recipe for endless war, writes Peter Dickinso', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putins-quest-to-reclaim-historical-russian-lands-is-a-recipe-for-endless-war/'}, {'signal_id': 'cf7f77bd43401708', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Rethinking political risk in Argentina: Why the next election may matter less than investors think <p>Argentina’s next election could shake markets even without reversing Milei’s reforms.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/rethinking-political-ris', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/rethinking-political-risk-in-argentina-why-the-next-election-may-matter-less-than-investors-think/'}, {'signal_id': '24932cdefceb268a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The Board of Peace for Gaza is not a commercial enterprise. It should stop acting like one. <p>The Board of Peace is missing the infrastructure, funding, and security guarantees it needs to make progress on its mission.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-board-of-peace-for-gaza-is-not-a-commercial-enterprise-it-should-stop-acting-like-one/'}, {'signal_id': 'b465cd68433e191e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How Far Could the Student List Reshape Serbia? | A Debrief With Misha Glenny <p>Europe Center Resident Senior Fellow Ilva Tare speaks with Misha Glenny to discuss Serbia\'s parliamentary results. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/balkans-debr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/balkans-debrief/how-far-could-the-student-list-reshape-serbia-a-debrief-with-misha-glenny/'}, {'signal_id': 'a7d346a295f59899', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How the Israeli election deadlock could end <p>The path ahead for either candidate in Israel\'s election to form a working coalition is uncertain. We polled our experts on what comes next. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/fast-t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/fast-thinking-how-the-israeli-election-deadlock-could-end/'}, {'signal_id': '9bd8e6cbb265e3af', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'For Russia, Trump’s diesel deal was just the first ask <p>The rationale behind the Trump administration’s recently issued General License 135 faces a number of questions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-russia-trumps-diesel-deal-was-just-th', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-russia-trumps-diesel-deal-was-just-the-first-ask/'}, {'signal_id': '6620381792a8ec02', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'UN report: Russian attacks on Ukraine’s power grid are a ‘crime against humanity’ <p>Russia’s bombardment of Ukraine’s civilian power grid qualifies as a crime against humanity, according to a new report by the UN’s Independent International Commission of Inquiry on Ukraine, writ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/un-report-russian-attacks-on-ukraines-power-grid-are-a-crime-against-humanity/'}, {'signal_id': 'd2320ec53d07edb6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'High oil prices have several Latin American governments feeling the financial pressure <p>Three charts show why oil prices that exceed 2026 budget assumptions matter for both importers and exporters.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/high-oil-pri', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/high-oil-prices-have-several-latin-american-governments-feeling-the-financial-pressure/'}, {'signal_id': '24e997d5aae2ae7b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'European infrastructure is vulnerable as Putin escalates Russia’s hybrid war <p>Putin is currently looking to exploit Europe’s vulnerabilities as he seeks ways to isolate Ukraine and cut off Kyiv’s European aid lifeline. Civilian infrastructure may be one of the continent’s weake', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/european-infrastructure-is-vulnerable-as-putin-escalates-russias-hybrid-war/'}, {'signal_id': '204bfadfb879faaf', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why France and Turkey are giving defense cooperation another go <p>France and Turkey still disagree on plenty, but Europe’s changing security environment is giving them stronger reasons to cooperate.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/fran', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/france-and-turkey-sign-2026-defense-roadmap/'}, {'signal_id': '616304587ab0c748', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The United States needs an energy policy investors can bank on <p>Unlocking long-term private investment in US energy infrastructure requires a federal policy framework driven by performance, not political preference.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/the-united-states-needs-an-energy-policy-investors-can-bank-on/'}, {'signal_id': '6852301af360f4c6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Any means necessary: Are courts safe in the digital age? <p>Reports are on the rise of hacks at federal courts in the United States, putting sensitive data, such as informants' identities, at risk. In litigation involving spyware, even more sensitive data is at risk. What protect", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/any-means-necessary-are-courts-safe-in-the-digital-age/'}, {'signal_id': '774544594e3a0d7c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Experts react: Serbia’s Vučić is out and the student-led movement is in. What comes next? <p>Serbia’s student-led opposition just ended Vučić’s fourteen years at the helm. Atlantic Council experts assess what comes next.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/di', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/experts-react-serbias-vucic-is-out-and-the-student-led-movement-is-in-what-comes-next/'}, {'signal_id': '830b870cf2cf7380', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Some reasons for hope in Israel’s sharply divided election <p>Regardless of the outcome, the end of campaigning could open chances for diplomacy that were previously closed. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/some-reasons-for-hope-in-israels-shar', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/some-reasons-for-hope-in-israels-sharply-divided-election/'}, {'signal_id': 'f3105e55b72fcd0e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Should Beijing be pushed to let the renminbi rise? <p>Can currency diplomacy address the global imbalances that have featured on both the Group of 7 and Group of Twenty agendas this year? And can the US and the EU finally align their strategies to tackle China's overcapacity? Bra", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/should-beijing-be-pushed-to-let-the-renminbi-rise/'}, {'signal_id': 'e8acc90d9099a0a0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Pakistan’s changing development assistance landscape: Manifestations, implications, and opportunities <p>Pakistan’s development assistance landscape is undergoing a major structural shift. Western bilateral aid is declining, multilateral development bank (MDB) financing is increa', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/pakistans-changing-development-assistance-landscape-manifestations-implications-and-opportunities/'}, {'signal_id': '9f36eae9d80182b8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Bangladesh’s changing development assistance landscape: Manifestations, implications, and opportunities <p>Bangladesh is absorbing one of the most severe aid shocks in its history while simultaneously benefiting from an unprecedented surge in remittances and multilateral developm', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/bangladeshs-changing-development-assistance-landscape-manifestations-implications-and-opportunities/'}, {'signal_id': 'e245bf27d8d46f75', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What Lula’s comeback\xa0win means for Brazil and beyond <p>Our experts unpack what Lula’s victory means for Brazil’s ties with Washington and how it could reshape a region trending right.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-lulas', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-lulas-comeback-means-for-brazil-and-beyond/'}, {'signal_id': 'fcabd6b594cc138b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The new EU Arctic strategy shows ambition—but also anxiety <p>While the United States is only referenced seven times in the document, elements of the strategy read as a response to Trump administration initiatives. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-new-eu-arctic-strategy-shows-ambition-but-also-anxiety/'}, {'signal_id': '3b49d0f3a48be7d4', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for the Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: Washington Must Learn From Its Own Successes <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-washington-must-learn-from-its-own-successes/">Charai for the Jerusa', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-washington-must-learn-from-its-own-successes/'}, {'signal_id': '692e700a7d608840', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What’s at stake in Israel’s first elections since the October 7 attacks? <p>An unclear outcome for Netanyahu or opponents could lead to prolonged coalition negotiations or even more elections. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/whats-at-stake-in-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/whats-at-stake-in-israels-first-elections-since-the-october-7-attacks/'}, {'signal_id': 'afbc585633f00659', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What will end Trump’s back-and-forth approach toward Russia and Ukraine <p>Can pressure from Congress and the American public push Trump to take a tougher stance against Putin?</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-will-end-trumps-back-and-forth', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-will-end-trumps-back-and-forth-approach-toward-russia-and-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'a796270d87a688aa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'North Korea may be the biggest winner of Russia’s war in Ukraine <p>Pyongyang is gaining combat experience, technology, and money by supporting Russia\'s invasion, raising security risks for the Indo-Pacific. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/nor', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/north-korea-may-be-the-biggest-winner-of-russias-war-in-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '3bf3ed10b9682fb0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What the new arrest warrant for Raúl Castro means for Cuba’s future <p>Washington’s latest pressure on the Cuban regime comes as Cuba’s economic and humanitarian crisis spirals from bad to worse.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-the-new-arr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-the-new-arrest-warrant-for-raul-castro-means-for-cubas-future/'}, {'signal_id': '1fdcc47c94964258', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Piasecki cited in Treaty and Talks on how AI can help create jobs in developing economies <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/piasecki-cited-in-treaty-and-talks-on-how-ai-can-help-create-jobs-in-develop', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/piasecki-cited-in-treaty-and-talks-on-how-ai-can-help-create-jobs-in-developing-economies/'}, {'signal_id': '333c3c4afcb6406f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Piasecki cited in Intelligence Report on Venezuela’s debt restructuring efforts <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/piasecki-cited-in-intelligence-report-on-venezuelas-debt-restructuring-efforts/">Piase', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/piasecki-cited-in-intelligence-report-on-venezuelas-debt-restructuring-efforts/'}, {'signal_id': '1a4cb617fd394393', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Piasecki cited in The Global Eye on the issues at stake at the IMF-World Bank meetings in 2026 <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/piasecki-cited-in-the-global-eye-on-the-issues-at-stake-at-the-imf-worl', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/piasecki-cited-in-the-global-eye-on-the-issues-at-stake-at-the-imf-world-bank-meetings-in-2026/'}, {'signal_id': '1d9537d29906bc2b', 'source': 'atlant